diff --git a/docs/api_to_audit.md b/docs/api_to_audit.md
index 9ade6aafb9..10a5e3309e 100644
--- a/docs/api_to_audit.md
+++ b/docs/api_to_audit.md
@@ -3433,3 +3433,11 @@
 
 Stabilization requires lifecycle coverage for reuse, missing paths, cleanup in
 progress, cross-project ownership, and concurrent creation before binding.
+
+## Browser Workbench native controls
+
+`ExperimentalPluginBrowserPage.experimental_workbench(action)` is optional on older desktops. The backend equivalent is `bb.sdk.experimental_desktopBrowsers.experimental_workbench(scopeAndAction)`. Actions are snapshot, set-permission, reset-permissions, clear-console and open-devtools. Permissions are scoped to a native tab and exact HTTP(S) origin, survive same-origin reload, and clear on cross-origin navigation or tab destruction. Media checks distinguish audio and video; third-party frames do not inherit grants. Unknown permissions stay denied. Editing permissions reloads to stop existing device streams. Native console history is capped at 200 entries with 2048-character message/source bounds; denied requests at 50. DevTools opens only on explicit action.
+
+Audit before stabilization: Electron permission-name/version coverage, per-device limitations (Web MIDI grants API access, not individual ports), persistent profile grants, native prompt UI, multi-window scoping, navigation races, console lifecycle, host protocol compatibility and desktop/web fallback.
+
+`set-graphics` saves desktop-wide settings for the next launch. Profiles are default, webgl-only (`WebGPUService` disabled), and webgpu-only (`disable-webgl`). Experimental web-platform features are a separate boolean. The snapshot distinguishes active and requested settings and reports restartRequired. Configuration is validated and atomically written under Electron userData; invalid input falls back to normal startup. It does not restart the desktop or force an application's renderer. Audit exact Chromium flag behavior on supported Electron releases before stabilization.
