diff --git a/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-browser.md b/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-browser.md
index 71d36538b0..bfa521f4db 100644
--- a/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-browser.md
+++ b/packages/templates/src/templates/bb-guide-browser.md
@@ -28,3 +28,9 @@
 All commands support JSON output. In plugin code use `bb.sdk.experimental_desktopBrowsers`; the Plugin Guide documents the typed surface. Stop/Take over revokes native control; stopping the owning thread also releases its server control leases. Old connection generations cannot control replacement windows.
 
 Cloud browsers are not supported. Headless Chrome on an enrolled host belongs to the Browser Automation plugin.
+
+### Native browser workbench
+
+`bb browser workbench TAB --host HOST --instance INSTANCE --generation GENERATION --thread THREAD [--json]` returns the tab's origin, effective permissions, recent denied requests, and bounded console history. `--action '{"kind":"set-permission","origin":"http://localhost:3000","permission":"microphone","decision":"allow"}'` changes one permission and reloads the page. Decisions: allow, block, default. Other actions: reset-permissions (requires origin), clear-console, open-devtools. Grants last for this tab and origin; cross-origin navigation clears them. Microphone and camera are separate. MIDI grants cover the API, not individual ports. Console content is untrusted page data. Open DevTools only when the user requests a visible window.
+
+`--action '{"kind":"set-graphics","settings":{"profile":"webgl-only","experimentalWebPlatform":false}}'` saves desktop-wide graphics settings for the next launch. Profiles: default, webgl-only, webgpu-only. The response distinguishes active/requested settings and restartRequired. Settings are stored in `browser-workbench.json` under Electron userData. It never restarts BB automatically and does not override unrelated external launch flags.
